The trigger delegates every event to the handler. The handler recalculates each affected account from an aggregate query over the database, so the totals stay correct across multiple DML statements in one transaction. It only updates accounts whose values actually change, and it ignores Opportunity updates that touch only fields it doesn't use. That second check stops the loop with the legacy `AccountTrigger`, which updates open opportunities whenever an account is updated.

