Notes on the design:
- The accumulator is a transaction-scoped static set. Both trigger chunks of a 250-record insert add to it, and the finalizer runs once at the end of the DML operation, so one job carries all 250 Ids.
- Each finalizer run drains the set, so two DML statements produce two jobs with only their own Ids.
- The finalizer returns without enqueuing when the set is empty. This covers DML on other sObjects and operations where no StageName changed.
- This assumes TAF runs DML finalizers in the same transaction as the trigger. That is how the framework is designed, but I have not checked the `FinalizerHandler.Context` internals because the reference file omits them. The finalizer does not depend on any Context field.
- `OpportunityErpSyncJob` is unchanged.

